Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_guid_survives_printing_and_parsing`.

The defect: `to_ascii` prints the first group in storage order instead of byte-reversed, while
`try_from_ascii` still reverses it. The printed form looks like a GUID and parses back to a
different one.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Guid::try_from_ascii(&g.to_ascii()), Some(g))`.

